      "writtenOn": "2023-09-15T13:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the service VM doesn\u0027t forward any specific error type to the HAL, so when the RKP VM fails, we always send STATUS_FAILED [1]. However, based on the HAL spec, we should send [STATUS_INVALID_MAC](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/security/rkp/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IRemotelyProvisionedComponent.aidl;l\u003d230;drc\u003d6aae9b643247f78d8f47c544a3d790f137d9341d) if the MAC validation fails. That requires the RKP VM to forward certain types of errors back to the host so that the HAL impl in the host can react accordingly.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/virtualizationservice/src/remote_provisioning.rs;l\u003d111;drc\u003d2628d332805c96198d598cc2698f312c7ebf627e",
      "parentUuid": "85f4cb57_7a5859a8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
